The two Hungarian checks are separate findings with separate gates. The
CLI's --hungarian enables both (hungarian_notation on the unprefixed
Count, hungarian_type_mismatch on sLabel := 0); --hungarian-types enables
only the type check (validate.go: CheckHungarianTypes = hungarian ||
hungarianTypes). Neither fires by default.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Mark;
	:DECLARE Count, sLabel;
	Count := 1;
	sLabel := 0;
	:RETURN sLabel + LimsString(Count);
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics [--hungarian] --
2:11-2:16 warning hungarian_notation: Variable 'Count' should use a Hungarian notation prefix (a, b, d, fn, n, o, s, v)
4:2-4:13 warning hungarian_type_mismatch: 'sLabel' promises a string by its prefix, but this expression produces a number - rename the variable or fix the expression
-- diagnostics [--hungarian-types] --
4:2-4:13 warning hungarian_type_mismatch: 'sLabel' promises a string by its prefix, but this expression produces a number - rename the variable or fix the expression
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Mark;
	:DECLARE Count, sLabel;
	Count := 1;
	sLabel := 0;
	:RETURN sLabel + LimsString(Count);
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
